<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Reichskommissariat Norwegen</h1><p class="st-meta">1940 CE – 1945 CE · capital Oslo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">German civilian occupation regime in Norway in 1940-1945, headed by Josef Terboven, with Vidkun Quisling's collaborationist government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> on 9 April 1940. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidkun-quisling">Vidkun Quisling</a>, leader of the fascist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasjonal-samling">Nasjonal Samling</a>, proclaimed himself head of government the same day, but the Germans soon pushed him aside. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-vii">King Haakon VII</a> and the government refused to surrender and went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, and in April 1940 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Hitler</a> appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josef-terboven">Josef Terboven</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichskommissar">Reich Commissioner</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josef-terboven">Terboven</a> held real power from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>, banning all parties except <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasjonal-samling">Nasjonal Samling</a>. In 1942 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidkun-quisling">Quisling</a> became Minister-President of a collaborationist government, which tried to Nazify schools and the church but met mass resistance from teachers and clergy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway's</a> resistance sabotaged the heavy water plant at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vemork">Vemork</a>, and in 1942 Norwegian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auschwitz-concentration-camp">Auschwitz</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> surrendered on 8 May 1945, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josef-terboven">Terboven</a> killed himself. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidkun-quisling">Quisling</a> was tried and executed in October 1945, and his name became a byword for traitor. The legal government returned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-vii">King Haakon VII</a> came home to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a> in June 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/reichskommissariat-norwegen.jpg" alt="Reichskommissariat Norwegen" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: German government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(1935%E2%80%931945).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1940 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Oslo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Josef Terboven, Vidkun Quisling</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Norwegian, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Reich Commissariat of Norway, Quisling regime</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1942&amp;focus=reichskommissariat-norwegen" aria-label="Reichskommissariat Norwegen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4905 169 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Reichskommissariat Norwegen lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5225 425L5225 425M5225 425L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5225 425h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5225 425h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Oslo. <a href="/atlas?year=1942&amp;focus=reichskommissariat-norwegen">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

